<ns0:section xmlns:ns0="http://xml.house.gov/schemas/uslm/1.0" status="repealed" style="-uslm-lc:I80" id="idb8c44b32-47c4-11f1-9a61-b1559996dfe8" identifier="/us/usc/t18/s283"><ns0:num value="283">[§ 283.</ns0:num><ns0:heading> Repealed. <ns0:ref href="/us/pl/87/849/s2">Pub. L. 87–849, § 2</ns0:ref>, <ns0:date date="1962-10-23">Oct. 23, 1962</ns0:date>, <ns0:ref href="/us/stat/76/1126">76 Stat. 1126</ns0:ref>; <ns0:ref href="/us/pl/100/180/dA/tVIII/s822/a">Pub. L. 100–180, div. A, title VIII, § 822(a)</ns0:ref>, <ns0:date date="1987-12-04">Dec. 4, 1987</ns0:date>, <ns0:ref href="/us/stat/101/1132">101 Stat. 1132</ns0:ref>]</ns0:heading><ns0:notes type="uscNote" id="idb8c44b33-47c4-11f1-9a61-b1559996dfe8">
<ns0:note topic="removalDescription" id="idb8c44b34-47c4-11f1-9a61-b1559996dfe8">
<ns0:p style="-uslm-lc:I21" class="indent0">Section, acts <ns0:ref href="/us/act/1948-06-25/ch645">June 25, 1948, ch. 645</ns0:ref>, <ns0:ref href="/us/stat/62/697">62 Stat. 697</ns0:ref>; <ns0:ref href="/us/act/1949-06-28/ch268/s2/b">June 28, 1949, ch. 268, § 2(b)</ns0:ref>, <ns0:ref href="/us/stat/63/280">63 Stat. 280</ns0:ref>, related to officers or employees interested in claims against the government. <ns0:ref href="/us/pl/87/849">Pub. L. 87–849</ns0:ref> continued limited applicability to retired officers of the Armed Forces of the United States. <ns0:ref href="/us/pl/100/180">Pub. L. 100–180</ns0:ref> repealed section to the extent that it had not been repealed by <ns0:ref href="/us/pl/87/849/s2">section 2 of Pub. L. 87–849</ns0:ref>. Section was supplanted by <ns0:ref href="/us/usc/t18/s205">section 205 of this title</ns0:ref>.</ns0:p>
</ns0:note>
<ns0:note style="-uslm-lc:I74" role="crossHeading" topic="statutoryNotes" id="idb8c44b35-47c4-11f1-9a61-b1559996dfe8"><ns0:heading class="centered"><ns0:b>Statutory Notes and Related Subsidiaries</ns0:b></ns0:heading></ns0:note>
<ns0:note style="-uslm-lc:I74" topic="effectiveDate" id="idb8c44b36-47c4-11f1-9a61-b1559996dfe8"><ns0:heading class="centered smallCaps">Effective Date of Repeal</ns0:heading><ns0:p style="-uslm-lc:I21" class="indent0">Repeal effective 90 days after <ns0:date date="1962-10-23">Oct. 23, 1962</ns0:date>, see <ns0:ref href="/us/pl/87/849/s4">section 4 of Pub. L. 87–849</ns0:ref>, set out as an Effective Date note under <ns0:ref href="/us/usc/t18/s201">section 201 of this title</ns0:ref>.</ns0:p>
</ns0:note>
</ns0:notes>
</ns0:section>
